* Process corners for
* benchmarks/design-agent/reference/rc-relaxation-oscillator/oscillator.spice.
*
* Self-contained, PDK-free stand-in for a real .lib (copy of
* examples/kb/rc-relaxation-oscillator/corners.lib -- see that file's own
* header): the two process knobs that actually set this oscillator's
* period are the timing capacitor value and the reference-derived charge
* current, so each section scales those rather than device models.
* Replace this file with a real PDK model library (e.g. sky130's
* sky130.lib.spice) once the oscillator is built out of real devices --
* see README.md's "Known limitations" note.

.lib tt
.param corner_cap=1.00
.param corner_iref=1.00
.endl tt

.lib ss
.param corner_cap=1.10
.param corner_iref=0.95
.endl ss

.lib ff
.param corner_cap=0.90
.param corner_iref=1.05
.endl ff
